  "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#semiotic_projection_1",
  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the rhetorical question and implied comparison in the scene",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material and the scene as a whole, which frames the viewer as someone who must evaluate the moral or cultural equivalence between alcohol bans in Islamic countries and the permissiveness of alcohol in Western countries. The rhetorical question 'shouldn't this be banned in western countries?' implicitly addresses the user, inviting them to consider their own cultural stance or values. The user is not explicitly projected onto a specific visual material (like the man or the keys) but onto the conceptual contrast established by the scene and text, which requires the user to position themselves in relation to the cultural comparison.",
